  "body": "What happens: `.github/scripts/post-merge-skip.sh` (`docs_only`, line 28) treats a push that changes only `site/*` paths other than `site/content/*` and `site/tests/*` as docs. The post-merge gate does not run for that push.\n\nThe site tests read `site/static/icons/`, `site/static/guide-pictures/`, `site/tools/` and the zola templates. The batch tier runs the site tests step since #4133. A push that changes only an icon in `site/static/icons/` can make the site red on `main`, and post-merge does not show it.\n\nExpected: a push that changes a path of `site_step::INPUTS` (`xtask/src/site_step.rs`) under `site/` runs the post-merge gate.\n\nMitigation now: the quick gate of the PR runs the site step for such a change, and the release tier at the cut runs it with a FAIL rule for a missing tool.\n\nThis is a `.github` change. It waits for the decision of the maintainer.\n\nFound while working #4133.\n\nDone means: `post-merge-skip.sh` does not skip a push that changes `site/static/*`, `site/tools/*` or `site/templates/*`, and `.github/scripts/test-post-merge-skip.sh` pins it.\n",
